OL,3,GNEWSARural pubs bear brunt of decline  
OL,4,Aas numbers fall by a fifth in 15 years 
OL,6,FAn Ayrshire pub landlord, forced to    
OL,7,Fclose his doors for good, says the     
OL,8,Ffinancial strain on the trade has      
OL,9,Fbecome "unmanageable".                 
OL,11,FMikey Lennon took over the King's Arms 
OL,12,Fin the village of Fenwick just 18 days 
OL,13,Fbefore the first Covid lockdown in     
OL,14,FMarch 2020. In June, he closed it.     
OL,16,FIt was Fenwick's only pub. Now, apart  
OL,17,Ffrom a hotel, it has none.             
OL,19,F"Costs just got too high, became       
OL,20,Funmanageable," he said.                
